<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Douglas Hyde</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1860">1860</a>–<a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Dubhghlas de hÍde</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Douglas Hyde was an Irish scholar of the Irish language and the first President of Ireland, from 1938 to 1945. In 1893 he co-founded the Gaelic League to revive the Irish language and culture, which inspired a generation of nationalists. A Protestant, he was chosen as an agreed candidate by the main parties.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/douglas-hyde.jpg" alt="Douglas Hyde" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Douglas_Hyde,_circa_1940.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
